  "version": "2.0",
  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "Intracranial EEG from 9 adults during a memory-guided actions experiment (preprocessed epochs, Moraresku et al.)",
  "description": "Preprocessed stereo-EEG epochs from 9 patients with drug-resistant epilepsy at the Motol Epilepsy Center in Prague, recorded during a delayed memory-guided action task. Each patient has 170 bipolar-referenced epochs spanning -2 to 7.9 s around encoding onset. Recordings cover the inferior parietal lobule, ventral temporal cortex and hippocampus. The dataset is a BIDS derivative that re-packages the authors' Zenodo release without further processing.",
  "methods_description": "Semi-rigid depth electrodes (DIXI Medical) were implanted for clinical pre-surgical evaluation. Signals were recorded at 2048 Hz with Quantum NeuroWorks amplifiers and downsampled to 512 Hz. A 50 Hz notch filter was applied with harmonics, faulty and seizure-onset-zone contacts were removed, and bipolar referencing was applied between adjacent contacts. In the delayed task, participants encoded the positions of two objects, waited through a delay, then reached with a joystick to the remembered position. Stimuli were presented with PsychoPy3, and task and iEEG were synchronised by TTL pulses.",
